  "body": "## What changed\n\nA setup that stands the part on its edge can now take \"What Setup1 leaves behind\" as its stock. The turn is a quarter turn about X or Y from the setup before it. Before this change the carry was refused by name (`CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL`).\n\n**camcraft-sim** (`crates/sim/src/stock_sim/carry_side.rs`, new):\n\n- `SideTurn` is one of the sixteen side-on quarter turns. `CarryTurn` is a lattice turn or a side turn.\n- `Body::carry_side` reads the column body again along the new tool axis:\n  - The level axis that stays level is re-indexed, centre onto centre.\n  - The old heights become slabs of one cell, centred on the old Z range. A face inside a slab counts the slab whole.\n  - The old level axis becomes the height. The top and the floor are the hull of the old column centres that hold material. Each end moves out to the next centre that holds no material, or to the lattice edge. A cavity between the ends is filled.\n- The carried body is never smaller than the body the columns hold. It is at most one grid cell larger on a turned face. The raw faces of a box stock at the lattice edge are read exactly.\n- The field engine refuses a side-on turn by name (`FIELD_SIDE_CARRY_REFUSAL`). The shipped engine is the column engine.\n- `CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL` has shorter words: \"the stock simulation carries machined stock only through quarter turns (steps of 90° about X, Y or Z)\". A turn off the quarter is still refused and the app still names the turn and the two setups.\n\n**camcraft-app**:\n\n- `stock_sim_carry.rs`: `carry_turn` returns a `CarryTurn`. The program walk judges the body before a side-on turn and keeps those gouges for the final verdict. The hull can hide a gouge that an earlier setup cut. This is the same fold that a block left for a new block gets (#320).\n- `side_on_note` adds a note line to the gate: the stock was turned side-on, and what the verdict reads.\n- `rest/across.rs` and `rest.rs` hold a `CarryTurn`. The rest reading, the judged stock, the prior plan and the carried block follow the same turn. The `Debug` text of a lattice turn is unchanged, so no shipped stamp moves.\n\nNo user-facing command is new. No MCP tool is owed.\n\n## How it was tested\n\nPinning tests:\n\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_carry_side.rs`\n  - `a_faced_plate_carries_side_on_with_its_volume_and_verdict` (the \"Done means\" test: volume, size, clean verdict, and a 1 mm gouge in Setup2 is found)\n  - `a_gouge_cut_before_a_side_on_turn_still_reads_in_the_verdict`\n  - `the_verdict_says_the_stock_was_turned_side_on`\n  - `the_field_engine_refuses_the_side_on_carry_by_name`\n- `crates/sim/tests/stock_carry_side.rs` (14 tests: exact block, steps on both sides, reversed axes, a filled cavity, a face inside a slab, a thin plate, there and back, the verdict, each refusal, the digest text)\n- `crates/app/tests/setup_stock_source.rs`: `a_side_on_turn_between_setups_carries_and_a_skew_turn_is_refused_naming_the_turn` replaces the #866 test that pinned the side-on refusal. The test count of the file is the same.\n\nMutation checks. Each line was removed or changed, the named test went red, the file was restored, and `cmp` against the backup was identical:\n\n| Line | Test that went red |\n|---|---|\n| non-finite refusal (`SideTurn::from_matrix`) | `turns_off_the_quarter_are_refused_by_name` |\n| off-quarter entry refusal | same |\n| not-a-permutation refusal | same |\n| mirror refusal | same |\n| not-side-on refusal | same |\n| field-engine refusal | `the_field_engine_refuses_a_side_on_turn_by_name` |\n| too-tall refusal | `a_body_too_tall_for_the_turned_lattice_is_refused_by_name` |\n| high-side pad (never short) | `a_step_turned_side_on_is_never_read_short` |\n| low-side pad (never short) | `a_step_on_the_low_side_is_never_read_short_either` |\n| floor flag dropped after the turn | `a_clean_block_turned_side_on_reads_no_gouge_and_no_judged_floor` |\n| slab counted whole | `a_face_inside_a_slab_counts_the_slab_whole` |\n| gouge kept before a side-on turn | `a_gouge_cut_before_a_side_on_turn_still_reads_in_the_verdict` |\n| side-on note on the gate | `the_verdict_says_the_stock_was_turned_side_on` |\n| note only for a side-on carry | same |\n| lattice-turn digest text | `the_two_kinds_of_turn_are_told_apart` |\n\nGate. `cargo xtask gate quick --dry-run` selected about 180 app suites, because the gate map of many suites names `sim::stock_sim`. The run was therefore done by name:\n\n- sim: every suite of the quick plan (the lib and 32 test binaries), all green.\n- app: the lib (313 tests) and `setup_carry_side`, `setup_stock_source`, `setup_carry`, `carried_verify`, `rest_across_setups`, `carried_engine_agreement`, `carried_fixtures_cache`, `carried_corner_rest`, `between_setups`, `setups`, `setup_align`, `stock_sim_document`, `post_not_judged`, `stock_engine_agreement`, `stock_view`, `fixtures`, `probe_only_sim`, all green.\n- ui: `cargo test -p camcraft-ui --lib setup_stock` (4 tests), green.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`, clean.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- The batch tier and the other app suites of the quick plan.\n- The pixel snapshots. No snapshot PNG changed.\n- Windows and macOS. The run was on Linux.\n- The prior plan on a job thread (`PriorPlan::simulate`) with a side-on turn. Its change is one call (`carry_through`).\n- A carried fixture at a turned face. See the known limits.\n\n## Known limits\n\n- A wall that the tool flank cut, or a step, is read up to one cell outside the real face after the turn. The verdict can show rest of up to one cell on a finished face. The carried-fixture law (#321) can refuse a fixture that touches such a face. The workaround is the setup's own stock. The follow-up issue for the exact carry is linked in the issue comments.\n- A cavity seen from the side is filled. Rest machining in the turned setup can cut air there. It never meets uncut material.\n- The verdict taken before the turn does not credit the edge breaks and marks of the earlier setup. The fold for a new block (#320) has the same limit.\n\nDecision record: `docs/decisions/874-side-on-carry.md`. Branch from upstream `main` at 6c33940d.\n\nChangelog: A setup turned side-on (a quarter turn about X or Y) can take the machined stock of the setup before it; the carried stock is never smaller than the real stock, and a gouge cut before the turn stays in the verdict.\n\nEffort: max (not escalated)\n\nFixes #874\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
